{
  "name": "How to Prepare for a Post-Storm Roof Inspection in Alvarado",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Prioritize Safety First",
      "text": "Before doing anything else, make sure your property is safe to approach. Look out for downed power lines, gas odors, or unstable trees. If there's any doubt about structural integrity, keep a safe distance and wait for professionals to arrive. Don't attempt to climb on your roof, especially if there's visible damage or wet surfaces. Your safety is paramount.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Document Everything You See (Safely!)",
      "text": "From a safe vantage point on the ground, take photos and videos of any visible damage. Capture wide shots of your property and close-ups of specific issues like missing shingles, dented gutters, or fallen debris. Make sure to note the date and time you took these. This initial documentation helps establish a timeline of the damage.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Clear the Immediate Area Around Your Home",
      "text": "If it’s safe to do so, remove any debris that's easily accessible on the ground around your home. This gives the inspector clear access to the roofline and ensures they can move around freely. You don't need to tackle large, dangerous debris, but clearing small branches or scattered items can be helpful.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Gather Any Relevant Information",
      "text": "Have your insurance policy information handy, along with the date and approximate time of the storm. If you have any records of previous roof repairs or installations, those can also provide valuable context for the inspector. Knowing your roof's history helps them differentiate between new storm damage and older wear.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Be Ready to Ask Questions",
      "text": "Once the inspector arrives, don't hesitate to ask about their process, what they look for, and when you can expect a report. A good inspector will be happy to explain their findings and guide you through the next steps. Being informed empowers you to make the best decisions for your home. When you're ready for a thorough post-storm roof inspection in Alvarado, reach out to Discounted Roofing Co. for expert assistance.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
